.TH SWAYDESK-BLUETOOTH-POPUP 1 2026-11-14 "swaydesk 0.1.6" "Sway desktop components"
.SH NAME
swaydesk\-bluetooth\-popup \- Bluetooth popup for Waybar
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B swaydesk\-bluetooth\-popup
.SH DESCRIPTION
Turns Bluetooth on and off, makes the computer visible, lists the paired devices, connects, disconnects, searches for and pairs new devices, shows details, forgets a device and sends files. It talks to BlueZ over D\-Bus. The search runs only on request and stops after 30 seconds.
.PP
Turning Bluetooth on first clears a software rfkill block (the airplane-mode key, \fBrfkill block\fR) through \fI/dev/rfkill\fR, like \fBrfkill unblock bluetooth\fR, without asking for a password; a hardware block is only reported. It never reads or types pairing codes: the blueman agent answers them in its own dialog. While pairing, the popup stays open, because BlueZ cancels the pairing when the program that asked for it closes.
.PP
Running it again while the popup is open closes it, and opening it closes the other popups of the bar. Esc, clicking outside or switching workspace also closes it.
.PP
The session runs it under the name waybar\-bluetooth\-popup (a link in the package's helper directory to /usr/bin/swaydesk\-bluetooth\-popup); the process name is waybar\-bluetooth\-popup too.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-check
Exit 0 at once without doing anything: the Python launchers use it to check that the binary and its libraries load.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/swaydesk/config.toml
The desktop configuration: language, accent color, GTK and icon themes, folder color, file manager, weather location and holidays.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR bluetoothctl (1),
.BR swaydesk (7)
